menu "Cockpit hardware"

choice COCKPIT_BOARD
    prompt "Panel board"
    default COCKPIT_BOARD_WAVESHARE_7B
    help
      Which Waveshare ESP32-P4 panel this firmware is built for. These boards
      are not interchangeable at runtime: they use different display
      controllers, resolutions, orientations and backlight/reset pins, so the
      board must be chosen at build time. Flashing the wrong one typically
      leaves the screen black, because the backlight GPIO of one board is
      unconnected on the other.

    config COCKPIT_BOARD_WAVESHARE_7B
        bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B (1024x600, EK79007)"
        help
          The 7B: a 1024x600 landscape EK79007 panel, backlight on GPIO 32
          (inverted), reset on GPIO 33. Mounted upside down, so the UI layer
          rotates 180 degrees.

    config COCKPIT_BOARD_WAVESHARE_LCD_X_7
        bool "Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-X, 7 inch (720x1280, ILI9881C)"
        help
          The X series 7-inch panel: a 720x1280 PORTRAIT ILI9881C, backlight
          on GPIO 26 (not inverted), reset on GPIO 27. Presented to the
          cockpit as a 1280x720 landscape screen, rotated in hardware by the
          P4's PPA. The 8-inch and 10.1-inch X panels use a different
          controller (JD9365) and are not supported yet.

endchoice

endmenu
